  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A deuteron and a proton moving with equal kinetic energy enter into to a uniform magnetic field at right angle to the field. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></math> are the radii of their circular paths respectively, then the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As we know, radius of circular path followed by charged particle under perpendicular magnetic field is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp; Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mi>q</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
